--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracker 0557. DECISIONS.md's 2026-09-01 ruling (refined same day)
gates the PDF path at roughly 40 pages, decided by a fallback chain rather
than one field, because the flat-cache form-feed signal alone is blind on
about 45% of cached PDFs (`4 708 of 8 590`, SPEC.md's extract-layer entry).

## Actions

1. Check whether Zotero's `indexedPages` field is exposed on the local API
   (unconfirmed as of the ruling -- this is the first thing to settle, and
   may kill the "first choice" tier if it turns out not to be reachable
   from zoteus's vantage point).
2. Use `totalPages` from the same response when present.
3. Otherwise load the accessible source PDF through pdf.js and use
   `PDFDocumentProxy.numPages`, without extracting page text.
4. Only when the PDF cannot be opened, treat `indexedPages`, literal page-break
   count, and the labelled character-count estimate as lower bounds, in that
   order. A lower bound may prove long and may never prove short.
5. If no source total exists and no lower bound reaches the threshold, report
   unknown and take the long-document-safe path.
6. Threshold: ~40 pages, from the author's acceptance-test statement
   (ticket 0028 log, 2026-09-01). Not separately re-argued for the
   estimated case per the ruling.

## Test

- Fixtures cover `totalPages`, pdf.js `numPages`, each cache lower bound, and an
  inaccessible source whose low lower bounds must yield unknown/long-safe rather
  than short. Assert the tier and certainty, not only the route.

## Invariants

- The gate always produces a safe route. Unknown takes the long-document path;
  it is never laundered into a short estimate.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `indexedPages` local-API reachability settled, one way or the other --
      reachable; evidence in the 2026-09-02 log entry
- [ ] all three tiers implemented and tested
- [ ] threshold configurable in one place, not hardcoded per call site
